  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** El Pollo Loco is riding a clear wave of demand improvement, with broad-based comparable sales growth driven by a return of lunch traffic, ongoing dinner strength, and emerging late-evening occasions. Product innovation is resonating with customers, and the brand’s transformation is lifting traffic and loyalty. The fast-casual backdrop appears supportive, and the chain is gaining competitive share in its core markets without obvious macro or regulatory headwinds.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing with growing confidence, raising the full-year outlook after a strong quarter underscored by operational gains and marketing discipline. CEO Liz Williams emphasized balanced daypart performance and a commitment to margin stewardship. The team is pairing near-term sales momentum with a longer-term vision of thoughtful, footprint expansion. The market’s positive reception to results and raised guidance suggests management’s credibility is strengthening as the brand transformation takes hold.",
